ive, pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. So we have same.\n\nWe also have note: Candidate A can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. No stress resilience, crew cooperation unknown, reliability unknown.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, puts concern for others above everything, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. So C has reliability, crew atmosphere positive, but communication issues.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills, moody, loner. So D has responsibility, problem solving, but crew cooperation issues.\n\nWe need to decide if we still vote B or maybe C? Let's weigh.\n\nCriteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility.\n\nB: reliability (very conscientious) good. Stress resilience (handles stress well) good. Technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills) good. Cooperation: can be grumpy, uncooperative, pretentious, wrong tone -> negative. Responsibility? Not explicit but conscientious suggests responsible. So B strong except cooperation.\n\nC: reliability (100% reliable) excellent. Stress resilience unknown. Technical competence unknown. Decision quality (quick correct decisions) good. Cooperation: creates positive atmosphere, puts concern for others above everything -> strong. Communication difficulty and egocentric are concerns, but positive atmosphere suggests cooperation? Might be contradictory. Not willing to further education -> adaptability concerns. So C strong on reliability and crew cooperation, but unknown stress and technical.\n\nD: responsibility serious